From c60623d42998c6e194b86e89091fd3f9005a0b48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leopold Li <leopold.lixiaoliang@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 18:01:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] revert(gateway): drop main-turn ACK; LLM response is the
 receipt
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to 67a6d59 based on WeChat test feedback.

Rationale
---------
The main-turn ACK "⏳ 处理中: ... (Working)" duplicated the LLM's own
streamed response. When A hits an idle session, hermes starts the agent
immediately; even a fast turn produces streaming output within seconds
which itself confirms receipt. The gateway-side ACK layered on top
looked like a duplicate message with no added information.

The queue-mode ACK stays — B/C queued during a busy turn have no other
signal until the drain fires, so the "📥 排队 #N: 'preview' (Queued)"
receipt still delivers real UX value there.

Analysis behind the decision
----------------------------
B and C ACKs are already async-independent from A's main turn:
  * Each inbound spawns its own _process_message_background task.
  * The session guard (_active_sessions[sk]) only serializes AGENT
    execution, not inbound handling.
  * _handle_active_session_busy_message + _maybe_send_queue_ack run
    on B/C's own tasks, awaiting only adapter.send.
So queue ACK latency is bounded by the platform send, not by whatever
A's agent is doing. No need for a wider always-queue refactor.

Revert scope
------------
Removed:
  * ``_maybe_send_main_turn_ack`` helper method.
  * ``busy_main_ack_enabled`` config → env bridge.
  * ``HERMES_GATEWAY_BUSY_MAIN_ACK_ENABLED`` env var support.
  * Invocation from ``_handle_message`` idle path.
  * ``TestMainTurnAck`` test class (5 tests).

Retained (from 67a6d59):
  * ``_msg_preview_for_ack`` helper — still used by queue ACK.
  * Queue ACK format: ``📥 排队 #{N}: "preview..." (Queued)``.
  * Updated queue-ACK test assertion.

Tests: 50/50 pass.
